<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahaus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahaus is a town in the Borken district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, close to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> border. Its moated baroque castle was a residence of the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Münster. After the secularisation of 1803 the district passed to the short-lived Principality of Salm, and later to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahaus.jpg" alt="Ahaus" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Stahlkocher assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahaus_Georgsbrunnen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
